{title: Groanings Too Deep For Words}
{subtitle: Romans 8:26–27}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]We groan inwardly in our [Eb]weakness
[Gm]Waiting for redemption of our [Eb]bodies
[Bb]We do not know what to [Eb]pray for
As we [Gm]ought in this [F]dark [Bb]place
[F/A]What to [Gm7]pray for, as [F]we are in this [Eb]dark place
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Gm]But the Spirit [F]helps us in our frail[Eb]ty
[Bb]He intercedes [F]for the saints
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm]With groanings too deep [Eb]for words
He prays to [Bb]the Father above
The Spirit intercedes [F]for us
According to God's holy [Eb]will
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]He who searches our [Eb]hearts knows
[Gm]The mind of the [F]Spirit is [Eb]clear
[Bb]He pleads on our be[Eb]half always
[Gm]For those who [F]are called by [Bb]name
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
With groanings too [F]deep for words
[Gm]He prays to the [Eb]Father above
[Bb]The Spirit intercedes [F]for us
According to God's holy [Eb]will
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]We wait [F]with patience [Eb]for what we [Bb]see [F/A]not
[Gm]Hope that is [F]un[Eb]seen sustains [Bb][F/A]us
[Gm]The [F]firstfruits of [Eb]the Spirit
[Gm]Lead [F]us to glory and [Eb]light
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]With groanings too [F]deep for words
[Gm]He prays to the [Eb]Father above
[Bb]The Spirit intercedes [F]for us
According to God's holy [Eb]will
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Groanings too [F]deep for words
[Gm]He intercedes for [Eb]the [Bb]saints
{end_of_verse}
